<title>HONG KONG: CEPA sees income doubling soon - paper.</title>
<headline>CEPA sees income doubling soon - paper.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The executive chairman of Consolidated Electric Power Asia Ltd (CEPA) has said new projects coming on line would double group income over the next couple of months, the Hong Kong Standard reported on Monday.</p>
<p>Gordon Wu was also quoted as saying he hoped to maintain management of CEPA after a sale of CEPA shares by Hopewell Holdings Ltd, of which Wu is managing director.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, Hopewell said it was considering sale of part or all of its stake in CEPA, which was about 60 percent.</p>
<p>There were five or six suitors wanting to buy into CEPA, Wu was quoted by the newspaper as saying.</p>
<p>The South China Morning Post reported him as saying that negotiations were approaching their final stage.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
